","updated_at":"2026-10-22T08:16:48Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":9,"created_at":"2025-01-30T22:34:18Z","updated_at":"2026-06-19T18:33:27Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102215","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102215","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102215.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102215.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"This is a continuation of https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101380 with additional changes as discussed in https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/11531, \"Standardize label for holes in heightfield collider data\"\r\n\r\nThis pull adds two methods to the physics server - `heightmap_shape_is_hole_label`, and `heightmap_shape_get_hole_labels`. Both methods are exposed to GDscript, and have been implemented for GodotPhysics and Jolt.\r\n\r\n`heightmap_shape_get_hole_labels` returns a list of heightfield values that the physics engine will interpret as holes when computing collision for a heighmap shape.\r\n\r\n`heightmap_shape_is_hole_label` is a convenience function that will return true if the value passed to it represents a hole.\r\n\r\nAs in the original PR, the logic used to triangulate heightmap collision shapes has been modified to support holes in the heightfield, testing points using `heightmap_shape_is_hole_label`.\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/031f24b0-b280-4121-ac4c-5be6e0452a3a)\r\n\r\n- *Production edit: This closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/2746 and closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/11531.*","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102215/reactions","total_count":8,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":3,"confused":0